ollowing statements are true?\n\n- $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $3$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-5$ of $A$\n- $v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $1$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-5$ of $A$\n- $v$ is an eigenvector corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-5$ of $A$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072860/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bc510ecdc71bb5f96baa6261e5189763e163378f4c7ed8623625e7bb07c1c41"} {"question" "q-109587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "A *generalized eigenvector* ${v}_{n}$ of rank $n$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda $ of a matrix $A$ is a nonzero vector such that\n\n$$\n{v}_{n}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{n-1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }…\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }{v}_{1}\\overset{A-\\lambda I\\,}{\\to }0,\n$$\n\nwhere ${v}_{n-1},{v}_{n-2},…,{v}_{1}\\ne 0.$ An *eigenvector* is simply a generalized eigenvector of rank $1.$\n\nFirst, we compute $A+5I:$\n\n$$\nA+5I=[\\begin{aligned}-6 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -7\\end{aligned}]+5[\\begin{aligned}1 & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\n- Next, we find the image of $v$ under the action of $A+5I:$\n\n$$\n(A+5I)v=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]={{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{w}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Since we got a nonzero vector, we now compute the image of $w$ under the action of $A+5I:$\n\n$$\n(A+5I)w=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]={{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}\\ne 0\n$$\n\n- Again, since we got a nonzero vector in the last step, we now compute the image of $x$ under the action of $A+5I:$\n\n$$\n(A+5I)x=[\\begin{aligned}-1 & 2 & -1 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2 \\\\ -1 & 3 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=0\n$$\n\nSo, we obtain the following chain of maps:\n\n$$\n{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{v}\\overset{A+5I\\,}{\\to }{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 2 \\\\ 2\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{w}\\overset{A+5I\\,}{\\to }{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{x}\\overset{A+5I\\,}{\\to }{{[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 0 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{0}\n$$\n\nHere, we see that $A+5I$ maps $v$ to $0$ in $3$ steps.\n\nTherefore:\n\n$\\,$ *$v$ is a generalized eigenvector of rank $3$ corresponding to the eigenvalue $\\lambda =-5$ of $A.$*\n\nSo, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072860/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bc510ecdc71bb5f96baa6261e5189763e163378f4c7ed8623625e7bb07c1c41"} {"question" "q-109587" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072860/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "1416c654aa8baecc8dce6610dc9d378a4b35ffe9031bf01424f120b94a680ed0"} {"question" "q-109587" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14072860/state.json" "file_sha256" "3bc510ecdc71bb5f96baa6261e5189763e163378f4c7ed8623625e7bb07c1c41"} {"question" "q-109587" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I only"] ["text" "II and III only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"] ["text" "None of the statements are true"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/